import java.util.Scanner;
public class nameandage {

	public static void main(String[] args) {
		
		Scanner sca=new Scanner(System.in);
		System.out.println("Enter a Name:");
		String a = sca.nextLine();
		System.out.println("Enter a Age:");
		int b = sca.nextInt();

	}

}

OUTPUT:
Enter a Name:
deepthi
Enter a Age:
20

DESCRIPTION:
A Scanner object named sca is created. It is initialized to read from the standard input stream (System.in), which refers to the console (keyboard input).
The nextLine() method is used to capture the entire line of text entered by the user. This will be the user's name and is stored in the String variable a.
